60,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,Option C is the only one that addresses the usage imbalance and the financial waste. It introduces a system of accountability.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Option C could work, provided it's not just for formal meetings, but for the conversations we've been avoiding.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,May,,"I'm leaning toward C. If it's bookable, we can stop paying those ridiculous hourly rates at the other place.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,I've seen the numbers. Option C is the only one that makes financial sense. The fit-out cost is a drop in the bucket.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,"A meeting space can be a place of growth, provided we remember to listen as much as we speak.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Jonathan, the ""human"" element you want is better served by a scheduled space than a chaotic one.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,Perhaps. As long as it doesn't become another sterile box where we only talk about deadlines.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,May,,"Let's just make sure the ""system"" doesn't mean I'm the one stuck managing the calendar for free.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, a simple digital calendar is hardly a burden. The real burden is the current waste of company funds.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,A shared calendar is a shared commitment. It teaches us to respect each other's time and space.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"I agree. A structured environment prevents the ""first-come, first-served"" anarchy that leads to the current mess.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I will support C, if we agree that it can be used for informal resolution of conflicts as well.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,May,,Deal. As long as it's fancy enough that we don't feel the need to leave the building.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,I'm satisfied. It solves the financial leak and provides a clear purpose. No more guessing.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Servas,,"When a space has a purpose, the people within it find their own. I am in agreement.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,Then we are in alignment. The evidence points to a single logical conclusion.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,It is a start. Let's hope it brings us closer than the desks do.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,May,,I'll be the one to pick the colors for the new furniture. I have a great eye for this.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"Just keep the cost within the quote, May. I'm not signing off on a designer lounge.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Servas,,Let us move forward with a spirit of cooperation and a commitment to cleanliness.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
